 succeeded in 737ms:
{"baseRefName":"main","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-30T23:11:19Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-30T23:11:19Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"feat(installer): make project installs transactional","oid":"c4131bd0964839409d2d132a358a0c1c623edab6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T00:41:35Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T00:41:35Z","messageBody":"The manager writes install marker schema 2 for every schema 1 through 6\nmutation, but protocol conformance compared that output against the\nsuite's expected/marker.json, which is frozen marker-v1 legacy-read\nevidence. The comparison could only ever fail on schema_version,\nbuild_roots and builds.\n\nRead the new expected/marker-v2.json writer golden instead, and fail\nclosed when a conformance root does not publish it rather than falling\nback to the legacy file. Legacy-read compatibility is now asserted on\nits own: expected/marker.json still parses as marker v1 and round-trips.\n\nBoth marker write sites used Path.write_text, which forwards\nnewline=None to TextIOWrapper and translates every LF to os.linesep, so\nWindows committed CRLF markers that could not equal the LF golden.\nserialize_install_marker now returns the exact bytes and both sites use\nPath.write_bytes.\n\nPin the conformance checkout to the curator-spec commit that publishes\nthe writer golden and advance EXPECTED_MANIFEST_SHA256 to that suite:\nthe rc.5 suite carries the old digest but no writer golden, so no root\ncould satisfy both.","messageHeadline":"fix(installer): commit install markers as canonical LF bytes","oid":"8a02e179fe35205490f081a7caa2e191b524e534"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T10:39:22Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T10:39:22Z","messageBody":"Windows failed every PR 16 cell while POSIX stayed green, on four platform\nfacts rather than transaction logic.\n\nos.stat synthesizes the execute bits from .bat/.cmd/.com/.exe file names and\nonly from a path, so a command shim reported 0o777 through lstat and 0o666\nthrough the handle used to read it, and the digest guard read that as the\ntarget changing mid-digest. Digests and guards now use the permission identity\nWindows can hold, which is unchanged behaviour on POSIX.\n\nWindows records a symlink's type on the reparse point, and a file link onto a\ndirectory cannot be traversed. A staged adapter link is dangling by\nconstruction, so deriving its type by resolving the destination made a file\nlink that later raised WinError 5. The type now comes from the link itself.\n\nNew Windows objects belong to the token owner, the Administrators group for an\nelevated administrator, so the manager owned neither the home it created nor\nthe artifact its own compiler produced. The manager now provisions a home it\ncreates and makes a fresh artifact private before publication; the guards\nthemselves are unchanged and an established home is never re-provisioned.\n\nThe build stub could only ever be published on a host that is not Windows; it\nnow derives its target and artifact path from the host.","messageHeadline":"fix(installer): make windows project installs transactional","oid":"7a66c73ebb30822df40c87856f2301f1f409b735"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T13:49:30Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T13:49:30Z","messageBody":"Every windows-latest cell passed after the four platform fixes and none of\nthem finished in a usable time: Python 3.11 took 2h18m43s against 14 minutes\nfor the same suite on main, install tests ran 76-247 seconds each, and Python\n3.12 was still running after three hours. Two independent fault-handler dumps\nlanded on one frame, so this was a hot path and not a hang.\n\n_validate_namespace_independence compares every namespace with every other one\nand canonicalised both operands per comparison, so its filesystem work grew\nwith the square of the namespace count, on every journal save and twice per\n32 KiB staging chunk. One install measured 750,620 canonicalisations and 182\nof its 210 seconds on macOS, where realpath is cheap; Windows opens a handle\nper path component to answer the same question.\n\nA namespace is now a probe that resolves its path, and reads its physical\nidentity, at most once per pass. The same install performs 12,575\ncanonicalisations and takes 27.9 seconds. Parts comparison, prefix\ncontainment and the samestat alias check still run for every pair, and a real\nOSError is still never cached, so the guard keeps its full reach.","messageHeadline":"fix(installer): make windows namespace validation linear","oid":"98ab7a2c6c1e4be6e7827f2aa29890fc99c2ac02"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T13:59:21Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T13:59:21Z","messageBody":"Resolving each namespace once per pass left the pairwise scan as the remaining\nsquare term: one install compared 364,635 pairs, and on Windows that had\nbecome the dominant cost once the canonicalisations were gone.\n\nTwo namespaces overlap when one names the other, when one contains the other,\nor when two spellings reach one physical object. Each of those is now a\nlookup: a dictionary keyed by the normalized parts, a probe of each\nnamespace's proper prefixes over that same dictionary, and a dictionary keyed\nby st_dev with st_ino, which is exactly what samestat compares. Path depth is\nbounded, so the pass now costs the namespace count.\n\nSame predicate, same rejections, same message shape, and the reported pair is\nstill a pair that genuinely collides. The install test that took 210 seconds\nbefore this bug was diagnosed takes 5.5.","messageHeadline":"fix(installer): index transaction namespaces instead of pairing them","oid":"32737a8b325506721f66a8b3d8e17f7f638c48d1"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T14:59:31Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T14:59:31Z","messageBody":"Provisioning has to know whether this call created the home, because only a\nhome it creates may be stamped private and an established one must fail closed\non ownership drift instead. mkdir(exist_ok=True) cannot answer that, so it had\nbeen rewritten as a plain mkdir with a bare except FileExistsError: return.\nThat is not what the flag does: CPython re-raises unless the name that already\nexists is a directory. Dropping the condition made a regular file, or a symlink\nto a missing directory, an acceptable manager home, created at no particular\nmode and without the Windows ownership stamp this code exists to apply. The\ncondition is restated explicitly, and five tests now cover every shape the path\ncan be in, with the two adopted ones as positive controls.\n\nMemoising the namespace probes and indexing them were two commits, and only the\nfirst had its cost contract pinned: restoring a pairwise scan over memoised\nprobes leaves both canonicalisation tests green while reinstating the\ncomparisons that were the dominant Windows term. Work per namespace is now\npinned directly, so equally spaced sizes must grow by equal steps.","messageHeadline":"fix(locking): fail closed on a manager home that is not a directory","oid":"f8b90a5edf9bef4ffabd42b2338f399fc07b0b42"}],"headRefName":"task/TASK-260720-3t8nr3-transactional-project-hybrid","headRefOid":"f8b90a5edf9bef4ffabd42b2338f399fc07b0b42","isDraft":false,"mergeCommit":{"oid":"c7dbd6daf6562a264275fca06b50a527bce236d4"},"number":16,"reviewDecision":"","state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:02:21Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650434","name":"Tests / Python 3.11 on ubuntu-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:06:09Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650136","name":"Tests / Python 3.12 on ubuntu-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:19Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:02:26Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650258","name":"Tests / Python 3.13 on ubuntu-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:02:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650299","name":"Tests / Python 3.14 on ubuntu-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:15Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:02:53Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650171","name":"Tests / Python 3.11 on macos-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:03:32Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650234","name":"Tests / Python 3.12 on macos-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:17Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:03:23Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650329","name":"Tests / Python 3.13 on macos-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:03:20Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650216","name":"Tests / Python 3.14 on macos-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:15Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:12:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650237","name":"Tests / Python 3.11 on windows-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:15:22Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650500","name":"Tests / Python 3.12 on windows-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:09:28Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650338","name":"Tests / Python 3.13 on windows-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:17Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:12:20Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190650510","name":"Tests / Python 3.14 on windows-latest","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:17Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:41Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91190649953","name":"Type check / mypy strict","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:00:21Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-31T15:15:59Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30641011440/job/91194322083","name":"Build artifacts","startedAt":"2026-07-31T15:15:30Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"}],"title":"feat(installer): make project installs transactional","url":"https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/pull/16"}

